"""Reviewed stainless fillister and nickel-copper cap screw references."""
import json
DATA=json.loads((W/'scripts/mil-spec-fillister-cap-data.json').read_text())
for root,data in DATA.items():
 file='Reference-'+root+'.html';fillister=data['kind']=='fillister';fine=data['thread_series']=='UNF-2A'
 if fillister:
  identity='MS35275 identifies passivated corrosion-resisting-steel machine screws with a drilled, slotted fillister head and UNC-2A threads. This table covers all 119 reviewed Table I dash numbers, 201–319, across 2-56 through 3/8-16. The drilled head, slot and material are part of the requirement.'
  keys=['part','thread','length','length_tolerance','head_diameter_limits','total_head_height_limits'];heads=['Part number','Thread','Length per drawing (in)','Length tolerance (in)','Head diameter limits A (in)','Total head height limits O (in)']
  measure='<p>L is measured from the bearing surface beneath the head to the screw tip. O is total axial head height, including the dome; H is the height of the straight head side. The head is outside the under-head length measurement.</p><p>The reviewed issue requires complete threads to within two threads of the head, or closer if practicable, for screws 2.00 inches long and shorter. Longer screws have a minimum 1.50-inch thread length. Overall screw length does not establish a fixed unthreaded grip.</p>'
  geometry=filtered(['Thread','Head side height limits H (in)','Slot width limits J (in)','Drilled hole diameter nominal (in)'],[[h(r[k])for k in ['thread','head_side_height_limits','slot_width_limits','drilled_hole_nominal']]for r in data['head_geometry']],'MS35275 head side slot and drilling dimensions')
  geometry+='<p>The drilled hole is approximately at right angles to the slot and may break through the slot bottom in the reviewed drawing. The hole diameter is nominal; the head-side and slot values are minimum–maximum limits. The full issue controls drilling location, tolerances, slot depth, radii and edge treatment.</p>'
  ordering='<p>MS35275-217 is a 4-40 screw with a 0.500-inch under-head length. MS35275-263 is a 10-24 screw with the same listed length. Do not carry a dash number from the carbon-steel MS35265 family into this stainless family.</p><p>The reviewed material note permits specified corrosion-resisting steel types, including 302, 303, 304, 305, 316 and 384, with a minimum ultimate tensile strength of 80,000 psi. The family name alone does not guarantee Type 316. Preserve any specific material and certification requirement on your drawing.</p>'
  related=chips([('Carbon-steel coarse drilled fillister screws','Reference-MS35265.html'),('Carbon-steel fine drilled fillister screws','Reference-MS35266.html'),('Machine-screw family directory','Reference-Family-machine-screws.html')])+'<p>MS35276 is the stainless fine-thread drilled-fillister family. Send its full designation for review; the MS35275 coarse-thread table does not establish an MS35276 conversion.</p>'
  heading=root+' stainless drilled-fillister screws.';title=root+' Drilled Fillister Screws | Threads & Dimensions'
 else:
  identity=root+' identifies nickel-copper-alloy hexagon-head cap screws with '+data['thread_series']+' threads and a plain finish. The reviewed material requirement is QQ-N-281 Class A with a minimum ultimate tensile strength of 80,000 psi. The protective-coating note specifies none.'
  identity+=' This table covers '+str(len(data['rows']))+' selected references across 1/4, 3/8, 1/2 and 5/8-inch nominal diameters, with under-head lengths through 3.000 inches.'
  if fine:identity+=' The reviewed MS35312A issue marks the entire family inactive for new design after 15 February 1973. These historical references support existing drawing callouts.'
  else:identity+=' Asterisked inactive-for-new-design dash numbers in the reviewed drawing are omitted. Other diameters and lengths are outside this selected table.'
  keys=['part','thread','length','length_tolerance','across_flats_limits','head_height_limits'];heads=['Part number','Thread','Length per drawing (in)','Length tolerance (in)','Head across flats limits F (in)','Head height limits H (in)']
  measure='<p>L is measured from beneath the head to the screw tip. H is axial head height and F is head width across flats. The listed F limits describe the head, not a wrench or socket acceptance range.</p><p>The reviewed minimum thread-length rule is twice nominal diameter plus 0.250 inch, with a separate positive allowance and short-screw provisions. A listed under-head length is not a fixed grip length or a claim of full threading. The governing issue controls thread length and runout.</p>'
  geometry=''
  ordering='<p>'+root+'-3 identifies a 1/4-'+('28'if fine else'20')+' screw with 0.500-inch under-head length. '+root+'-109 identifies a 1/2-'+('20'if fine else'13')+' screw with 1.000-inch length. Use the complete series and dash number; matching the dash number alone does not preserve thread pitch.</p><p>Nickel-copper alloy, passivated stainless steel and plated carbon or alloy steel are different requirements. A common thread and head envelope does not establish an approved material or strength substitution.</p>'
  other='MS35311'if fine else'MS35312'
  related=chips([(other+' nickel-copper '+('coarse'if fine else'fine')+' threads','Reference-'+other+'.html'),('Stainless MS35307/MS35308 cap screws','Reference-MS35307-MS35308.html'),('Grade 5/8 hex cap screw families','Reference-Family-hex-cap-screws.html')])
  heading=root+' nickel-copper '+('fine'if fine else'coarse')+'-thread hex cap screws.';title=root+' Nickel-Copper Hex Cap Screws | Thread Sizes & Dimensions'
 rows=[[h(r[k])for k in keys]+['<a href="Quote.html?reference='+file+'&amp;part='+h(r['part'])+'">Quote '+h(r['part'])+' →</a>']for r in data['rows']]
 table='<p>Reference selections for identification and quotation. Webson confirms availability by inquiry; these rows do not indicate stocked inventory.</p>'+filtered(heads+['Request pricing'],rows,root+' reference screw dimensions')
 table+='<p>All dimensions are in inches. Printed decimal lengths such as 0.188, 0.312, 0.438 or 0.562 are retained where listed. The length tolerance column shows separate positive and negative allowances; these are not symmetric ± limits. Head dimensions are minimum–maximum drawing limits.</p>'
 sections=[('Identify the head, material and thread','<p>'+identity+'</p>','PART IDENTIFICATION'),(root+' part-number and dimension table',table,'REFERENCE SIZES'),('Measure length and head geometry',measure,'MEASUREMENT GUIDE')]
 if geometry:sections.append(('Check the slot and drilled head',geometry,'HEAD DETAILS'))
 sections += [('Read the complete part number',ordering,'ORDERING DETAILS'),('Compare related screw families',related,'FAMILY COMPARISON'),('Match the governing drawing issue','<p>Dimensions summarize '+h(data['reviewed_issue'])+'. These are selected historical references for purchasing identification. Later amendments or notices may apply. The issue required by your drawing controls full geometry, thread, material, finish and inspection requirements. A successor standard name does not automatically authorize a part-number change or substitution.</p>','DRAWING REQUIREMENTS')]
 guide(file,title,heading,'Look up '+root+' threads, under-head lengths and head dimensions. Filter the reference sizes and request a quote for the complete part number.',sections)
